body:
@Rindbee here's the thing, if you can't duplicate a scene with the changes you made with a command called `duplicate` where everyone expects it to do what it's supposed to, what's the point of having duplicate at all then?

For my project to work for the time being I replaced duplicate calls to instantiate and literally doing the whole updating the object again to match what should be a copy of it, counte-productive to say the least.

Last but not least, `duplicate` ACTUALLY used to duplicate everything in all Godot versions prior 4.2, with some caveats of course but it used to work as expected for most users.
